WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.694
Asha has felt tired for five days.

00:00:02.694 --> 00:00:04.849
Today, she’s going to the clinic.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.258
Before she leaves, she opens NikTan on her phone,

00:00:09.258 --> 00:00:12.327
chooses her language, and agrees to a screening.

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:15.261
Five short checks build a picture.

00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:19.500
Her camera estimates her pulse and checks her eye for signs of pallor.

00:00:20.336 --> 00:00:24.883
She follows a turning E, then listens for digits through background noise.

00:00:25.961 --> 00:00:29.781
In her own words, she adds what the camera can’t see.

00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:30.823
How she feels.

00:00:31.586 --> 00:00:33.798
Her health card brings it together.

00:00:33.798 --> 00:00:38.222
In this example, it suggests seeing a doctor today in General Medicine.

00:00:39.086 --> 00:00:41.476
A queue token tells her two people are ahead.

00:00:42.368 --> 00:00:45.902
At the clinic, the same visit appears on the triage board.

00:00:45.902 --> 00:00:49.115
Staff can see who is waiting and who needs attention.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.628
Her doctor opens the card.

00:00:51.628 --> 00:00:54.796
The screening gives their conversation a place to start.

00:00:55.492 --> 00:01:00.471
Across the hospital, staff can follow waiting times and department activity.

00:01:01.118 --> 00:01:03.878
After the visit, Asha photographs her prescription.

00:01:03.878 --> 00:01:06.910
She can compare the reading with the original

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.792
and ask her pharmacist about unclear words.

00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:14.151
At home, Thali helps her explore the nutrients in a meal.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.901
She can ask the assistant for help,

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:20.621
rate her visit, or check service availability.

00:01:21.274 --> 00:01:25.200
One visit, from her phone to her care team. NikTan.
